\label{FiniteOut}
Let $\mathcal{G}_\Gamma$ be a graph product of cyclic groups. Then $\mathrm{Out}(\mathcal{G}_\Gamma)$ is finite if and only if the following conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\Gamma$ has no SILs;
    \item $\Gamma\setminus\mathrm{st}(v)$ is connected for every $v\in V(\Gamma^\infty)$;
    \item if $\mathrm{lk}(u)\subset\mathrm{st}(v)$ and $o(u)=\infty$, then $o(v)<\infty$.
\end{enumerate}

